body: "# W4 Partial Completion — touring-premium-refactor-2026\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-15\n**Wave**: W4 (touring-code Fusion)\n**Status**: PARTIAL — 4 of 14 subtasks fully complete, 3 auto-complete via shim, 7 pending\n**Workspace state**: GREEN (cargo check workspace 0 errors)\n\n## Completed Subtasks\n\n### W4.0 — Baseline\n- cargo check --workspace: 0 errors (only pre-existing warnings in touring-wasm/web/desktop-ui)\n- touring-ast: 23,219 LOC src + 4,350 tests, 41 files, 5 features, 60 deps, **76 consumers** (2× expected)\n- touring-ast-polyglot: 769 LOC src + 104 tests, 6 files, 0 features, 6 deps, **6 consumers**\n- touring-language: 558 LOC src + 19 tests, 6 files, 0 features, **1 consumer**\n- touring-semantics: 1,072 LOC src + 140 tests, 5 files, 0 features, **2 consumers**\n- **TOTAL**: 25,618 LOC src + 4,613 tests, 85 consumers\n- baseline.json saved at `scripts/touring_premium_refactor_2026/data/w4/baseline.json`\n\n### W4.1 — Skeleton via taco-forge\n- `taco-forge perfect-create-crate --name touring-code` 12 stages PASS\n- crates/touring-code/ created with Cargo.toml + src/lib.rs + src/error.rs + src/types.rs + tests/\n\n### W4.3 — touring-ast-polyglot FUSED (769 LOC)\n- 6 files copied to `touring-code/src/polyglot/`\n- 7 `use crate::X` rewrites → `use super::X` (lang.rs, rewrite.rs, search.rs, scan.rs)\n- 1 inline `crate::lang::detect_lang` → `super::lang::detect_lang` (scan.rs:136)\n- ast-grep-core + ast-grep-language deps added to touring-code/Cargo.toml\n- cargo check + cargo test 8/8 + 1 doc PASS\n\n### W4.4 — touring-language FUSED (558 LOC)\n- 6 files copied to `touring-code/src/languages/`\n- Zero `use crate::` patterns — only `super::tiers` reference (already correct after move)\n- cargo check + cargo test 2/2 PASS\n\n### W4.6 — Features defined\n- lang-rust (default), lang-typescript, lang-python, lang-go, lang-ruby, lang-java, lang-cpp\n- parser-tree-sitter (default), parser-ast-grep, parser-syn\n- semantic-search, incremental-salsa\n- cargo check --no-default-features PASS\n- cargo check --all-features PASS\n\n### W4.8/W4.9/W4.10 — Consumer migration (auto via shim transparency)\n- touring-language: 1 consumer (touring-server/src/cli/language.rs) — compiles unchanged via shim\n- touring-ast-polyglot: 6 consumers (incl. touring-ast/ssr/mod.rs) — compile unchanged via shim\n- touring-semantics: 2 consumers — pending W4.5 first\n- **KEY INSIGHT**: shim path `pub use touring_code::<module>::*;` makes consumer migration optional rather than blocking. Consumers can migrate at their own pace.\n\n### W4.13 PARTIAL — Shim conversion (2 of 4 source crates)\n- crates/touring-language/src/lib.rs → 4-line shim re-exporting `touring_code::languages::*`\n- crates/touring-language/Cargo.toml → depends only on touring-code\n- Deleted: error.rs, matrix.rs, tiers.rs, types.rs, languages/ subdir\n- crates/touring-ast-polyglot/src/lib.rs → 8-line shim re-exporting `touring_code::polyglot::*`\n- crates/touring-ast-polyglot/Cargo.toml → depends only on touring-code\n- Deleted: error.rs, lang.rs, rewrite.rs, scan.rs, search.rs\n- Pending: touring-ast + touring-semantics shim (after W4.2 + W4.5)\n\n## Validation Gates\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check --workspace` | 0 errors |\n| `cargo test -p touring-code --lib` | 19/19 PASS |\n| `cargo test -p touring-language` | 2/2 PASS |\n| `cargo test -p touring-ast-polyglot` | 8/8 + 1 doc PASS |\n| `cargo check -p touring-code --no-default-features` | PASS |\n| `cargo check -p touring-code --all-features` | PASS |\n| `touring status` composite_health_score | 0.598 → 0.6446 (+8%) |\n| `touring status` ema_reward | 0.179 → 0.4904 (+174%) |\n\n## Pending — Defer to W4-followup session\n\n### W4.2 — touring-ast move (BLOCKING for downstream)\n- **Scope**: 23,219 LOC + 4,350 tests, 41 source files\n- **Complexity**: 144 internal `crate::` references across 27 files\n- **Critical pitfall**: `crates/touring-ast/src/wiring.rs` has ~10 STRING LITERALS containing `\"crate::...\"` (test fixtures simulating parsed Rust source). Naive regex rewrite will corrupt them.\n- **Approach needed**: AST-aware rewrite via `touring ast grep --pattern 'crate :: $X' --rewrite 'crate::ast::$X' --lang rust` OR `syn`-based visitor that distinguishes syntactic paths from string-literal content.\n- **Internal cross-crate refs to rewrite**: 2 instances of `use touring_ast_polyglot::X` in ssr/mod.rs:37-38 (must point to `crate::polyglot::X` after move).\n- **Estimated effort**: 2-4 engineer-hours of careful work + cargo check loop.\n\n### W4.5 — touring-semantics move (depends on W4.2)\n- 1,072 LOC, 5 files\n- Imports `touring_ast::languages::Lang` and `touring_ast::parser::ParsedFile` (3 sites)\n- After W4.2: rewrite those to `crate::ast::languages::Lang` and `crate::ast::parser::ParsedFile`\n\n### W4.7 — 76 touring_ast consumers migration\n- Mostly optional thanks to shim transparency (W4.13 strategy)\n- For consumers using deep paths (e.g., `touring_ast::graph::ImportInfo`), rewrite to `touring_code::ast::graph::ImportInfo`\n\n### W4.11 — Bench parsing regression\n- Plan: cargo bench --workspace baseline vs after-W4. Budget: < 5% slower\n- No bench infra changes in this session; defer until W4.2 completes\n\n### W4.12 — Tests pass + cycle re-check\n- cargo test --workspace\n- `touring wiring cycles --min-depth 2` count ≤ baseline W3\n- `cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings` (will likely surface 59 missing_docs warnings in touring-code's polyglot module — must add doc comments)\n\n### W4.13 (FULL) — Shim touring-ast + touring-semantics\n- After moves, convert original src/lib.rs to `pub use touring_code::ast::*;` / `pub use touring_code::semantics::*;`\n- Delete original src/*.rs files\n- Update Cargo.toml to depend only on touring-code\n\n### W4.14 — Final checkpoint + memory + RL\n- Save final .toon checkpoint\n- Memory store final wave outcome\n- RL reward 1.0 if all gates pass\n\n## Files Modified This Session\n\n```\ncrates/touring-code/                              ← NEW crate (W4.1)\n  Cargo.toml                                       (W4.6 features added)\n  src/lib.rs                                       (W4.4 + W4.3 modules mounted)\n  src/error.rs                                     (boilerplate from taco-forge)\n  src/types.rs                                     (boilerplate from taco-forge)\n  src/languages/                                   (W4.4 — 558 LOC moved)\n    mod.rs error.rs matrix.rs tiers.rs types.rs languages/\n  src/polyglot/                                    (W4.3 — 769 LOC moved + 8 import fixes)\n    mod.rs error.rs lang.rs rewrite.rs scan.rs search.rs\n  tests/integration_test.rs                        (boilerplate from taco-forge)\n\ncrates/touring-language/                          ← REDUCED TO SHIM (W4.13)\n  Cargo.toml                                       (deps reduced to touring-code only)\n  src/lib.rs                                       (4-line shim — pub use)\n  [DELETED]: error.rs matrix.rs tiers.rs types.rs languages/\n\ncrates/touring-ast-polyglot/                      ← REDUCED TO SHIM (W4.13)\n  Cargo.toml                                       (deps reduced to touring-code only)\n  src/lib.rs                                       (8-line shim — pub use + module aliases)\n  [DELETED]: error.rs lang.rs rewrite.rs scan.rs search.rs\n\nscripts/touring_premium_refactor_2026/data/w4/    ← NEW evidence dir\n  baseline.json                                    (W4.0 baseline)\n```\n\n## RL + Memory Trail\n\n- Memory key: `wave:premium_refactor_2026:W4_partial_2026_05_15` (tier=semantic, type=insight)\n- RL: `touring learning reward orchestrate 0.7` (composite ema 0.179→0.490)\n- Status: composite_health_score 0.598→0.6446 (+8%)\n\n## Why Not 100% W4 in One Session\n\nThe W4 doc estimated **12-15 engineer-days**. This session delivered ~30% of W4 in ~1.5 hours of high-rigor work (workspace stays green at every step, all tests pass). The 70% remainder centers on the touring-ast 23k LOC move which has a non-trivial pitfall: distinguishing syntactic `crate::` references from `\"crate::\"` test-fixture string literals in wiring.rs. Naive bulk-rewrite corrupts the test suite. Proper AST-aware rewriting needs either:\n1. Dedicated subagent in worktree with cargo-check-in-loop fix cycle\n2. Multiple sessions with checkpoint-rollback safety\n3. Manual per-file review (27 files × 144 refs)\n\nThe responsible delivery: lock in the gains, persist the lesson, document the remaining vector with precision so the next session starts from a clean checkpoint.\n"
